    "6a2fb62f-79e7-42de-acea-4e5fab243fb0": {
      "type": "columns-1",
      "blocks": {
        "12d522a9-b741-4d4c-9b79-bb469c9fa36d": {
          "type": "dropdown",
          "settings": {
            "reveal": false,
            "title": "Retreat Commitment & Payment Policy",
            "text": "",
            "dropdown_text": "<p><strong>🔖 The retreat payment is non-refundable. </strong></p><p>Participation in this retreat is confirmed immediately upon payment.</p><p>Because space is limited, <strong>all retreat payments are non-refundable</strong>. Once your payment is received, your spot is secured and cannot be transferred or refunded.</p>",
            "dropdown_image_fill": true,
            "background_color": "#01b4b4",
            "text_color": "#ffffff"
          }
        },
        "8b288a22-fe25-4939-a8bc-2bd82abe3281": {
          "type": "dropdown",
          "settings": {
            "reveal": false,
            "title": "Inclusions",
            "text": "",
            "dropdown_text": "<p>Specialized Sound Bath + Audio Recording for attendee to take home.</p><p>Hike at Cathedral Rock + One of the most Powerful Energy Centers.</p><p>Group Lunches, and Group Dinners on .</p><p>Spiritual Alchemy Workshops with Sarah Elkhaldy - The Alchemist:</p><ul><li>Alchemy + Esoteric Science Masterclass</li><li>Shadow Work Workshop</li><li>Authentic Cacao Ceremony</li><li>Exploring the Quantum Field with Susan Hassen - Spiritual Healer</li></ul><p>1 Rare Alchemical Elixir.</p><p>Group Dinner at Chocolate Tree.</p><p>Custom Alchemy Folder.</p>",
            "dropdown_image_fill": true,
            "background_color": "#01b4b4",
            "text_color": "#ffffff"
          }
        },
        "88fe273d-dad8-4fcb-8e72-e298aeffea83": {
          "type": "dropdown",
          "settings": {
            "reveal": false,
            "title": "Exclusions",
            "text": "",
            "dropdown_text": "<ul><li>Flights to and From Sedona, AZ</li><li>Hotel Stay</li><li>Meals, outside of those outlined above</li><li>Transportation to the Opening Ceremony</li></ul><p>📍Rooms are not covered in the retreat fee and must be booked by the attendee.<br/><br/>🌿 <strong>Travel Note</strong><br/>For those arranging accommodations, please note that the <strong>Green Tree Inn</strong> is the closest hotel to the <strong>Sedona Retreat Center</strong>, where we’ll gather on Friday, Saturday, and Monday for all-day workshops and shared meals.</p><p>If you’d like the ease of walking to the retreat center each morning, consider staying at the Green Tree Inn for added convenience.</p>",
            "dropdown_image_fill": true,
            "background_color": "#01b4b4",
            "text_color": "#ffffff"
          }
        },
        "dropdown_BKGM6C": {
          "type": "dropdown",
          "settings": {
            "reveal": false,
            "title": "Retreat Waiver",
            "text": "",
            "dropdown_text": "<p><em>Please review the waiver below provided by our trusted retreat partner. By making full payment, attendees acknowledge and agree to the retreat waiver as a condition of participation in The Alchemist Retreat.</em><br/></p><p><strong>ASSUMPTION OF RISK, WAIVER OF LIABILITY, AND CONSENT TO USE LIKENESS AGREEMENT </strong></p><p><strong>      </strong>This Assumption of Risk, Waiver of Liability, and Consent to Use Likeness Agreement (the “Agreement”) is entered into and made effective as of the date of your signature below (the “Effective Date”) by and between the signatory to this Agreement (the “Attendee”) and Sarah Elkhaldy, a sole proprietorship aka The Alchemist, organized and operating under the laws of the state of California (referred to herein as “The Alchemist”). Attendee and The Alchemist are referred to herein collectively as the “Parties”. </p><p> </p><p><strong>RECITALS </strong></p><p><strong>        WHEREAS, </strong>Attendee has signed up for and will be attending the Alchemy Retreat in Sedona, Arizona between November 20th – 24th, 2025 (the “Retreat”); </p><p>      <strong>WHEREAS</strong>, the Parties now wish to enter into this Agreement in order to confirm the limited rights, obligations, and responsibilities between the Parties as well as account for the at-your-own-risk nature of the Retreat. </p><p><strong>NOW THEREFORE</strong>, in consideration of the mutual promises set forth below, the Parties agree as follows:  </p><p> </p><p><strong>AGREEMENT</strong></p><p>1.     <strong>ASSUMPTION OF RISK</strong>. </p><p>a.      Although attending the Retreat is not inherently dangerous, Attendee may be exposed to certain risks during the Retreat, including but not limited to during the hike, during the sound bath, or while consuming foods, which include, but are not limited to falling, tripping, food sickness, and other injuries. </p><p>b.     By Attending the Retreat, Attendee hereby freely assumes the above-mentioned risks, as well as other risks not listed herein, and agrees that he/she is attending the Retreat under his/her own free will despite these risks.  </p><p>c.      Attendee hereby acknowledges and agrees that no part of the Retreat is required, and that should Attendee not be comfortable doing one or more activities during the Retreat, such as a hike, Attendee can withhold himself/herself from parting in any activities Attendee is either not comfortable doing or is not able to do. </p><p> </p><p><strong>2.     FOOD/HEALTH DISCLAIMER. </strong></p><p>a.      While the general risk of an adverse reaction to food/drink is generally small, you may have an underlying health condition, allergy, or sensitivity unknown to The Alchemist that could cause or contribute to an adverse reaction of some kind while consuming food or drink during the Retreat. </p><p>                             i.     This specifically includes the cacao ceremony in which you are given the option to consume a cacao-based drink. If you are unsure about your ability to consume the cacao-based drink during the cacao ceremony based on the effects of the cacao bean or your own underlying health condition(s), we recommend that you speak with a doctor before leaving for the Retreat. </p><p>b.     Attendee hereby acknowledges and agrees that if Attendee has a known allergy, sensitivity, or health issue unknown to The Alchemist, that it is Attendee’s sole responsibility to inquire into any food given or consumed to determine if consuming said food/drink would cause a reaction. In addition, since food will prepared by third-parties, The Alchemist cannot accept responsibility for any negligence on the part of the food-service provider. </p><p> </p><p><strong>3.     TRAVEL AND ACCOMMODATION DISCLAIMER. </strong></p><p>a.      Although traveling to the Retreat or staying in your chosen accommodation is not inherently dangerous, Attendee may be exposed to certain risks of travel and which include but are not limited to car accident, negligence on behalf of the driver, theft or other injury. Since the driver(s) and hotel(s) are be third-parties and not agents of The Alchemist, The Alchemist cannot accept responsibility for any negligence or issues related to these third-parties.</p><p> </p><p>4.     <strong>WAIVER OF LAWSUIT/LIABILITY</strong>. </p><p>a.      Attendee hereby releases The Alchemist and its owners, employees, and agents (the “Released Parties”) from any and all liabilities, causes of action, claims, and demands that arise in any way related to my injury, loss, harm, or similar that occurs to me during the Retreat, including transportation to and from the Retreat. This release also extends to claims of negligence. </p><p>b.     Attendee also agrees not to sue the Released Parties for any injury, loss, or harm that occurs before, during, or after the Retreat, subject to appliable law. </p><p><strong> </strong></p><p>5.     <strong>CONSENT AND USE OF LIKENESS. </strong></p><p>a.      Attendee understands and agrees that during the Retreat, Attendee may be photographed or videotaped and hereby fully gives Attendee’s consent to being photographed or videotaped. </p><p>b.     To the fullest extent permitted by law, Attendee waives all rights of publicity or pre-approval in connection with the use of Attendee’s likeness. </p><p>c.      By attending the Retreat and signing this Agreement, Attendee grants to the Alchemist its affiliates and related companies and persons the right to use my likeness, in whole or in part, in any form, without restriction, including promotional and marketing purposes on all mediums. </p><p><br/></p><p>6.     <strong>LIMITATION OF LIABILITY</strong>. </p><p>a.      THE RETREAT AND ALL ACTIVITIES PLANNED DURING THE RETREAT ARE PROVIDED 'AS IS' AND, TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, THE ALCHEMIST AND ITS OWNERS, DIRECTORS, EMPLOYEES, AND AGENTS EXCLUDE ALL REPRESENTATIONS OR WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO, IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, SATISFACTORY QUALITY, AND FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE. </p><p>b.     THE ALCHEMIST SHALL NOT BE LIABLE TO YOU FOR INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES RESULTING FROM ATTENDING THE RETREAT, EVEN IF THE ALCHEMIST WAS ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGES, NOR SHALL THE ALCHEMIST BE HELD LIABLE FOR DELAY OR FAILURE IN PERFORMANCE RESULTING FROM CAUSES BEYOND OUR REASONABLE CONTROL. IN NO EVENT SHALL OUR TOTAL LIABILITY TO YOU FOR ALL DAMAGES, LOSSES AND CAUSES OF ACTION EXCEED THE TOTAL AMOUNT YOU PAID TO ATTEND THE RETREAT. </p><p>7.     <strong>CHOICE OF LAW</strong>:  </p><p>a.      The Parties agree that the laws of the State of California will apply to this Agreement, without giving effect to its choice of law provisions. </p><p>b.     Any dispute arising out of or in connection with this Agreement shall be subject to binding arbitration in California, through JAMS. </p><p><strong> </strong></p><p>8.     <strong>MISCELLANEOUS.</strong></p><p>a.      By signing this Agreement, Attendee hereby represents and warrants that Attendee has read this Agreement in its entirety and understood the inclusions herein. Attendee either had this Agreement reviewed by an attorney or waived Attendee’s ability to do so. </p><p>b.     If any provision of this Agreement shall be held to be invalid or unenforceable for any reason, the remaining provisions shall continue to be valid and enforceable.  </p><p></p><p></p><p><strong>IN WITNESS WHEREOF, </strong>I agree to be bound by all of the terms and conditions found in this Agreement by making the full payment to The Retreat. </p>",
            "dropdown_image_fill": true,
            "background_color": "#01b4b4",
            "text_color": "#ffffff"
          }
        },
        "8fef7e85-3dbd-4573-b556-4afbf969813d": {
          "type": "dropdown",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "reveal": false,
            "title": "Waiver of Responsibility",
            "text": "",
            "dropdown_text": "<p>I, the undersigned participant, acknowledge that my participation in the \"The Viking Initiation | Norway 2023\" event (hereinafter referred to as the \"Event\") hosted by Yager Transformation Group, LLC, a Delaware limited liability company (the “Company\"), involves known and unanticipated risks and hazards. These risks include, but are not limited to, physical or emotional injury, paralysis, death, and damage to myself, to property, or to third parties. I understand that such risks cannot be completely eliminated and may be caused by varying conditions such as terrain, facilities, temperature, weather, lack of hydration, physical condition of participants, equipment malfunctions, vehicular traffic, and actions of others, including but not limited to, participants, volunteers, spectators, event officials, event monitors, and/or producers of the Event.<br/></p><p>Assumption of Risks<br/><br/>I affirm that I fully understand the nature and extent of the risks involved in the Event. By signing this form, I voluntarily agree to accept and assume all risks, both known and unknown, inherent or otherwise, associated with my participation in the Event. I assume full and complete responsibility for any injuries, damages, losses, liabilities, costs, or expenses that I incur as a result of participating in the Event.</p><p>Health Declaration<br/><br/>I hereby certify that I have either:<br/><br/>(a) undergone a comprehensive physical examination and have been given medical clearance by a qualified healthcare provider to participate in the Event; or<br/>(b) chosen to participate in the Event without seeking medical advice and clearance.<br/></p><p>I acknowledge and accept full responsibility for this decision and its potential implications. I hereby release, discharge, and covenant not to sue the Company and all other parties affiliated with the Event, including but not limited to, its parent companies, affiliates, subsidiaries, event organizers, sponsors, event directors, officials, contractors, advertisers, volunteers, staff, agents, representatives, and each of their respective insurance carriers, underwriters, subrogated agents, successors, and assigns (collectively, \"Releasees\"), from any and all liability, claims, demands, legal actions, and causes of action whatsoever, arising out of or related to any loss, damage, or injury, including death, that may be sustained by me or to any property belonging to me, related to such a decision, whether arising from the negligence of the Releasees or otherwise.<br/></p><p>Waiver of Liability and Indemnification<br/><br/>In consideration for allowing my participation in the Event, I voluntarily agree to the following:<br/><br/>(A) To waive, relinquish, discharge, release, and covenant not to sue the Company and Releasees from any and all claims arising from or related to any direct, indirect, incidental or consequential damages, injuries, losses, or death that I may suffer as a result of my participation in the Event.<br/><br/>(B) To indemnify and hold harmless the Company and Releasees against any and all legal claims, actions, suits, procedures, costs, expenses, damages, and liabilities,<br/>including attorney's fees, arising out of or related to my actions or conduct during the Event.<br/><br/>(C) To consent to receive medical treatment, including but not limited to first aid or emergency medical services, as may be deemed advisable in the event of injury, accident, and/or illness during the Event. I acknowledge and understand that I will be responsible for any and all medical and related bills that may be incurred as a result of any medical treatment for me.<br/><br/>Governing Law and Broad Interpretation<br/><br/>This Accident Waiver and Release of Liability Form shall be construed broadly to provide a release and waiver to the maximum extent permissible under the applicable law of Delaware. I certify that I have read, understood, and voluntarily agree to the terms stipulated in this document.<br/></p>",
            "dropdown_image_fill": true,
            "background_color": "#2e2767",
            "text_color": "#ffffff"
          }
        },
